WEBVTT

NOTE Paragraph boundaries measured from synthesis; timing within paragraphs is approximate.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.906
Secure code review examines whether
implementation preserves expected security

00:00:04.906 --> 00:00:09.143
properties. Relevant material includes
routes, dependencies, authentication

00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:13.324
middleware, authorization logic, input
handling, and sensitive operations.

00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:16.544
A model can explain unfamiliar
structures, locate checks,

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:21.007
and propose paths from an input to a
database operation or privileged function.

00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:25.300
Those paths guide investigation rather
than establish defects by themselves.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.965
Consider object authorization.

00:00:26.965 --> 00:00:31.406
A function accepting an object identifier
may appear to lack an ownership check.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.182
The reviewer must inspect
its callers, middleware,

00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:38.068
and data-access restrictions
to determine where ownership is enforced.

00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:41.121
Distinguish authentication,
which establishes identity,

00:00:41.121 --> 00:00:44.008
from authorization to access
this particular object.

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:48.283
A credible candidate identifies the
relevant identities, object relationship,

00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:51.780
execution path, and control
that appears absent or ineffective.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.590
Source analysis and dynamic testing
answer complementary questions.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.854
Code explains possible behavior;
an authorized test observes behavior under

00:00:59.854 --> 00:01:04.630
a particular deployment and configuration.
A test plan can vary permitted identities

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:09.008
and object relationships, checking both
expected success and expected denial.

00:01:09.008 --> 00:01:12.306
Record the actual response
and any resulting state change.

00:01:12.306 --> 00:01:15.718
One successful request without
the surrounding authorization

00:01:15.718 --> 00:01:19.300
context is not enough to demonstrate
an access-control failure.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.369
AI can draft these test cases,
interpret scanner output,

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:26.259
and help document reviewed paths,
including areas that remain untested.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:30.150
Application and API assessment also
needs business context that generic

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.986
tools may miss, such as which users
may perform a sensitive operation.

00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:38.040
Combine static reasoning with focused
execution evidence. Further study in

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.369
secure code review or web application
assessment develops this technical depth.

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:46.260
It helps distinguish a plausible
candidate from a demonstrated finding.
